 ## Event-driven supervision
 
 A zero-token bash watcher (`bin/fm-watch.sh`) sleeps on the fleet, classifies detected wakes in bash, and wakes the first mate only when something is actionable.
-Actionable wakes include captain-relevant status signals, no-verb signals whose crew is not provably working, authenticated check output such as PR merge polling or a Relay mention, stale panes whose crew is not provably working whether their status log looks terminal or non-terminal, provably-working stale panes that persist past `FM_STALE_ESCALATE_SECS` with neither their own task worktree being written nor their own pipeline step recording recent activity, declared external waits and verified captain-held transfers that remain declared past their current recheck interval, and heartbeat backstop hits.
